  "review": [
    {
      "section": "time.clock",
      "confidence": "medium",
      "note": "Replaced digit placeholders with the standard learner-course Cornish (SWF): feminine hour numerals agreeing with 'eur' (unn, diw, teyr, peder, pymp, hwegh, seyth, eth, naw, deg, unnek, dewdhek); '{h} eur' on the hour; 'X mynysen wosa {h}' / 'kwarter wosa' / 'hanter wosa' for past; 'X mynysen dhe {next_h}' / 'kwarter dhe' for to; 25 minutes as 'pymp mynysen warn ugens'. Compromise: 'dhe' triggers soft mutation of the following numeral (dhe dhiw, dhe deyr, dhe beder, dhe bymp, dhe dheg, dhe dhewdhek), which the single hours list cannot express, so the to-phrases use unmutated numerals. Not checked against a native source, so a Cornish reviewer should confirm."
    }
  ]
